From c826990e83260434315df8a234eda3dc3a1c86d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: askimi <44218719+RNI4114@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 09:09:11 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] intel: 16x16 cooperative matrices for D3D12 WMMA (FSR4)
 in wave32

D3D12 WMMA, as vkd3d-proton translates it, runs 16x16 matrices on one
32-wide subgroup and converts between u8 storage and f16/f32 math with
loops over the element index, expecting element i of a u8 matrix to be
element i of the f16/f32 matrix of the same use.

- 16x16 matrices narrower than the DPAS type of their use (8-bit A/B,
  8/16-bit accumulators) use that type's field width, so each invocation
  holds the same rows and columns whatever the element size; their loads
  and stores go element by element and same-use conversions are element
  wise.
- Stop advertising 16x16x16 with an f16 accumulator (that accumulator is
  widened and cannot feed DPAS).

The stacked two-DPAS muladd already works at SIMD32 on Jay. Verified with
fs4-xmx/tests/wmma32 (bit exact at subgroup 16 and 32).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
